    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d662">

                <pb facs="0813" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg739"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/607a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d662-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-22T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 22, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For your information, under the direction of the President no passports will be
                    issued to Socialists intending to attend the Stockholm conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d662-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d662-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also to the Ambassadors in France, Italy, Russia, and Spain and the
                    Ministers in Belgium, Denmark, the Netherlands, Norway, Sweden, and
                    Switzerland.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
